# A function value of an unbounded function type that gives a blueprint, applied by a
# line of a widget block; the value is a widget with places, named and not applied,
# given where the unbounded function type is asked (Type System ch. 2: a function is a
# value, and a blueprint is a value a function may give; ch. 5: a bounded function is
# given where an unbounded one is asked; Semantics ch. 8: "a blueprint builds nothing
# until a block applies it", then at the applying block's next positions).
# sem-ch08-widget-parameter-call-argument with the function type unbounded and the
# value taken out of an option. Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch;
# subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@Row: fn Nat -> @unit
fn @Row n:
    Ui.Label($text=$"row {n}")

?Keep: fn (unbounded fn Nat -> @unit) -> ?(unbounded fn Nat -> @unit)
fn ?Keep F = ? F

@Page: @unit
@Page:
    match ?Keep @Row:
        ? F: F 1
        nil: Ui.Label($text=$"none")
    Ui.Label($text=$"below")
